Subject: [PATCH 07807/11362] [outer-loop] ARC lever #2: goal-exemplar grading
 closes GAP-ARCH-GOAL-NOT-VERIFIED (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-4)

The goal-consistency veto in execute_bounded_llm_reinduction only fires when the
grading window has a real level-up, but the toward-next-level window has zero (the
per-boundary episode-transition-start reset), so a correct-dynamics/WRONG-win-
predicate model is trusted at a deepening boundary. Fix (exp4020 insight, default
off via CARNOT_ARC_GOAL_EXEMPLAR_GRADING): inject the already-captured prior-level
win-state grid as one synthetic ground-truth positive so the veto becomes
informative (predicate must return True on a real win state). Oracle-distinct (the
predicate never reads the level counter). Default-off -> byte-identical scored
behavior; submitted-agent parity 22/22 green; 4 unit tests; ruff+mypy clean.
Offline A/B on bp35/lf52/sc25 (gate: >=1 new level-up, no regression) is the
separate GPU measurement step.

